    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="b9774b96-4461-5586-8bf0-91628922a19a" activityNameId="d3844761-b858-5ee4-85e6-71320aad58f5" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Natural gas, production RU, at evaporation plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Natural gas, production RU, at evaporation plant
In 2019 90% of the imported Russian natural gas to RER was imported by pipeline and 10% as LNG. An average distance of 4300 km is estimated for the pipeline export from Russian Federation, of which are 410 km offshore pipeline. The estimated shipping distance for LNG are 11700 km.;
eb1c7c39-afca-3902-a88f-8d488a7a5da0
This dataset describes the transport needed for an average export of Russian natural gas. Gas losses and emissions during seasonal storage are included.
Location:  The data for storage emissions are based on global data. The amount of gas stored is a rough estimate based on European data. The average weighted transport distance is based on the trade movements 2019.
Technology: The distance is an European average based on the European long-distance pipeline network and LNG shipping routes.
Time period: Transport modes investigated for 2019.
Production volume: none
Sampling: Literature. Online calculators for distances.
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_eb1c7c39-afca-3902-a88f-8d488a7a5da0.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
